{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Archimedean.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.eventually_not_screen_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.eventually_not_screen_pow","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L279-L293","doc":"**Non-vacuity at every threshold** (Archimedean `K`): for `0 ≤ z < 1`\nand `t > 0`, every geometric-decay family `B·z^m` is rejected for all\nsufficiently large `m`, whatever the finite threshold `lam ≥ 0`.  The\nthreshold only moves the first rejected index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.not_screen_pow_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.not_screen_pow_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L267-L277","doc":"Rejection of the geometric family `B·z^m` is upward closed in `m`:\nonce `lam·B·z^n < t`, every `m ≥ n` is rejected. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:order-of-magnitude-screen","label":"prop:order-of-magnitude-screen","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.mul_prod_lt_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.mul_prod_lt_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L258-L265","doc":"Same, for an arbitrary finite family of downward factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.mul_pow_lt_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.mul_pow_lt_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L249-L256","doc":"**Direction obstruction.**  A base `B > 0` corrected by any number of\ndownward factors `0 ≤ z ≤ 1` never reaches a target `t > B`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.additive_admits_below","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.additive_admits_below","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L240-L245","doc":"The additive band admits the entire downward region `[0, t]`, so it\ncannot detect any \"too small\" (z < 1) direction error. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.operational_test_not_sufficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.operational_test_not_sufficient","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L228-L238","doc":"**Counterexample** to \"the operational test |F − t|/t > 10 is a\nsufficient condition for failure\" (proof.md, \"The gate\") on SIGNED\nvalues: `F = −19/2`, `t = 1` fails the additive test yet its\nmagnitude `19/2` lies inside the decade window. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.additive_of_screen_of_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.additive_of_screen_of_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L219-L226","doc":"On nonnegative magnitudes, window-pass implies additive-pass\n(so additive-rejection is sufficient for window-rejection there). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.additive_iff_le_of_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.additive_iff_le_of_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L208-L217","doc":"On nonnegative magnitudes the additive band is exactly a one-sided\nupper bound `x ≤ (lam + 1)·t`: it rejects nothing that is too small. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.additive_admits_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.additive_admits_zero","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L201-L206","doc":"The additive band admits `0` (no signal) whenever `lam ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.screen_ladder_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.screen_ladder_prod","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L187-L197","doc":"**Finite precision-ladder bound.**  For any finite family with\n`|a k| ≤ 1/2`, the product `∏ (1 + a k)` passes the screen around\n`1` at threshold `∏ (1 + 2|a k|)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.screen_one_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.screen_one_add","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L170-L185","doc":"A single ladder factor `1 + a` with `|a| ≤ 1/2` is within\n`1 + 2|a|` of `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.ne_of_not_screen_of_screen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.ne_of_not_screen_of_screen","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L157-L166","doc":"**Conditional rejection soundness.**  If the true value `xstar`\npasses at some threshold `mu ≤ lam` (HYPOTHESIS — for the Q_β\ngate this premise is a comparison with a CODATA number and is not\nestablished by this file), then every candidate value rejected at\n`lam` differs from `xstar`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.screen_prod_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.screen_prod_one","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L135-L153","doc":"Finite products: if each nonnegative factor `f i` is within `r i`\nof `1`, the product is within `∏ r i` of `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.screen_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.screen_mul","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L106-L133","doc":"Closed under products (nonnegative data): thresholds multiply.\nNo sign hypothesis on `lam` is needed: with `a, b ≥ 0` a negative\nthreshold forces `a = b = 0`, and the product screen holds trivially. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.screen_trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.screen_trans","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L91-L104","doc":"Multiplicative transitivity (nonnegative data): thresholds multiply. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.screen_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.screen_symm","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L83-L89","doc":"Symmetric (for a nonnegative target): `x` is within `lam` of `t`\niff `t` is within `lam` of `|x|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.screen_abs_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.screen_abs_iff","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L79-L81","doc":"The screen sees only `|x|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.screen_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.screen_refl","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L73-L77","doc":"Reflexive for `lam ≥ 1`: the target itself always passes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.not_screen_anti","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.not_screen_anti","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L67-L71","doc":"Contrapositive: rejection at `lam'` implies rejection at every\nsmaller threshold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.screen_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.screen_mono","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L60-L65","doc":"Monotone in the threshold: passing at `lam` implies passing at\nevery `lam' ≥ lam`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.AdditiveScreen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.AdditiveScreen","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L53-L56","doc":"The additive band used by the corpus siblings\n(`DirectionSanityGateClass`, `MassDirectionSanityGateClass`,\n`BarEvenKernel.direction_match`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.Screen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.OrderOfMagnitudeScreen.Screen","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/order-of-magnitude-screen.lean#L49-L51","doc":"The multiplicative order-of-magnitude window with threshold `lam`\naround target `t`: `t ≤ lam·|x|` and `|x| ≤ lam·t`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}